Author: claude
Blocked-by: 0691

--- log ---
2026-09-06T09:10Z claude created
2026-09-06T09:10Z claude note Filed out of 0694's placement review. 0694 asked for the scoped form and 0691 does not carry it; without this ticket the requirement would close with 0691 and lose its owner. Scoped to the wording only -- placement is settled by the same-day ruling in DECISIONS.md.

--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 0694 reviewed where the sitter button belongs and, in doing so, gave
the reason the coverage label needs a scope prefix. The button sits in the
items toolbar, whose scope is one library and one collection, while the
number it shows -- how much of the index is built -- is global background
work. The author's ruling keeps the button there. DECISIONS.md, same day:
the scope mismatch "is real and survives this ruling as a wording problem,
to be fixed in the tooltip rather than by moving the icon."

Ticket 0691 replaced the sitter's SDT jargon with plain language and settled
on "Index 43 %". Its vocabulary table pins that unscoped form, its acceptance
criteria never mention a prefix, and PR #369 ships it as written. So the
prefix is nobody's work until it is filed, which is what this ticket does.

The scoped form 0694 names is:

    Library: My Library — Index 43 %

Where it belongs is part of the work, not a given. The toolbar label is a
narrow strip and 0691 chose its wording for that strip; the tooltip and the
accessible name are the surfaces 0694 identified as able to carry the longer
string in either toolbar position. Ticket 0686 wants a stable accessible
name, so whatever this ticket writes into `aria-label` has to satisfy 0686
too rather than fight it.

## Relevant files

- `bench/sdt-sitter/bootstrap.js` -- builds the toolbar label, its tooltip
  and its accessible name. Moves to `plugins/sdt-sitter/` under ticket 0697;
  rebase onto whichever path is current when this ticket runs.
- `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py` -- 0691's source-anchored wording tests, one per
  template site. The new assertion joins them.
- `tickets/0691-sitter-plain-language-vocabulary.erg` -- the vocabulary table
  this extends.
- `tickets/0686-*.erg` -- the stable-accessible-name requirement the
  `aria-label` must keep satisfying.

## Actions

1. Decide which surface carries the scope: tooltip, accessible name, or both.
   Say why in the commit message; the toolbar strip itself is 0691's and does
   not have to grow.
2. Name the library from Zotero's own library record, not a hardcoded
   "My Library" -- a group library must read as itself.
3. Extend 0691's vocabulary table with the scoped form, so one table remains
   the whole vocabulary.

## Test

A source-anchored test in `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py` asserting the chosen
surface carries the library name in front of the coverage figure, scoped to
that site's block rather than the whole file, in 0691's style. Run it against
the unfixed tree first: it must fail, and it must fail because the prefix is
absent, not because the block moved.

A test that greps for the literal "My Library" would pass on a hardcoding and
is the wrong test -- assert that the label is built from the library record.

## Verification

- [ ] The new test is red before the change and green after.
- [ ] A group library shows its own name, not "My Library".
- [ ] `make check` green.

## Invariants

- 0691's toolbar wording stays as ratified unless this ticket rules
  otherwise on the record; this is an addition, not a revision.
- 0686's accessible name stays stable across state transitions.
- Placement does not change: the button stays in the items toolbar.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The coverage figure reaches the user with its library scope attached,
      on a surface named in the commit message.
- [ ] The library name comes from Zotero, not from a literal.
- [ ] 0691's vocabulary table records the scoped form.
